From 252c31c45f6f5e5a84dbd9b439a11cd2947d42cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:01:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 195/206] analyze_snapshot: add the four DD options theirs
 registers

--compute_dd_slot_mapping, --dd_table_data, --dd_caller_links and
--dd_function_identity, with roles read out of their main rather than
inferred from the names:

  * --dd_caller_links is an OUTPUT next to --compute_dd_table (their
    Dart_ComputeDDTable's second output pair) and an INPUT, required,
    next to --compute_dd_slot_mapping.
  * --dd_table_data is the table input, required for the slot mapping.
  * --dd_function_identity is the optional third input: the file
    gen_snapshot --print_dd_function_identity_to writes. Without it
    every FunctionKey is zero and the mapping is the bare 9-byte header.
  * --compute_dd_slot_mapping emits a DDSlotVoters stream (magic, two
    FunctionKey::WriteToStream per row, vector<SlotVoter>), which
    gen_snapshot --dd_slot_mapping accepts by its magic sniff.

Both "is required with --compute_dd_slot_mapping" errors are theirs
verbatim, in their order, after VM init.

Caller links: {caller self_hash, table position, callee position}, where
the callee list is per external branch in instruction order with
duplicates (FunctionAnalysisData+0x70), not the sorted JSON callees.

Two fixes to the table path the links exposed (table bytes unchanged):
  * BuildEntries now feeds the sort from an unordered_set of the cut
    nodes, as theirs does; this decides equal-hash positions.
  * The kind filter moved from inside CascadeLimiter::Run to after it:
    their Run cuts stubs too and filters while walking the cut set.

Oracle, ours-on-ours vs theirs-on-theirs, hello/base_dd/prog: ddt, ddcl
and ddsm byte-identical (cmp -l 0), with and without an identity file
(ddsm 25263 / 25263 / 91685 bytes); ddt+ddcl also identical at nine
budgets 1..100000 on hello and prog. A perturbed caller-links input
moves both outputs identically. Inputs that do not parse are refused
(rc 255, nothing written) where theirs crashes (rc 138).

Not reproduced, stated in code: --dd_table_data's effect on the --out
dumps (a warning is printed), and its role as Dart_ComputeDDTable's
input (no effect measured on two probes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

